WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Let's walk through the whole architecture.
These boxes are responsibilities;

00:00:04.016 --> 00:00:06.240
they do not require eleven new products.

00:00:06.366 --> 00:00:10.800
Follow one banking test
from a request to reviewed evidence.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.560
This is a proposed design
and an authored testing scenario,

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.800
not a report of a live
client implementation.

00:00:17.313 --> 00:00:20.880
Start with the engineer.
A payment provider accepts a transfer,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.440
but the customer sees
a timeout and retries.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.480
The test must prove that the retry
creates one transfer and one balanced

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.120
journal, not two debits.
The product owner and domain tester

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:37.387
approve that expected behavior
before AI drafts anything.

00:00:37.861 --> 00:00:42.160
Delivery systems supply the source
material: the payment story,

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:47.200
API contract, repository
revision and previous defects.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.760
Azure Boards or Jira can hold the story;

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:53.120
GitHub or Azure DevOps
can hold the code and pipeline.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:57.760
The important output is a traceable set
of versions, not a particular vendor.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.920
The context service selects the material
this task is allowed to use.

00:01:02.107 --> 00:01:06.160
It removes unnecessary data
and records an input snapshot.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.920
For our retry test, that
includes the idempotency rule,

00:01:09.964 --> 00:01:13.440
provider behavior
and relevant test helpers.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.053
Missing or contradictory requirements
go back to a person for clarification.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.040
The quality engineering
runtime turns that context into

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.840
a plan and a proposed test change.

00:01:24.053 --> 00:01:28.720
It records the model and prompt versions,
with limits on retries and resource use.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.480
A coding assistant can draft
a JUnit test with REST Assured.

00:01:33.568 --> 00:01:37.813
That draft still needs review;
it cannot redefine the payment rule.

00:01:38.261 --> 00:01:41.680
Next, the action gateway
checks the requested operation,

00:01:41.726 --> 00:01:46.640
target environment and approval. It can
permit a test run in the approved sandbox.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.720
A request outside that scope
is stopped or escalated,

00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:54.640
with a recorded reason.
Permission comes from this control,

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:57.000
not from the model saying
that an action is safe.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:02.440
The sandbox runs the real payment service
and database against controlled fixtures.

00:02:02.528 --> 00:02:07.120
Testcontainers can provide isolated
resources; WireMock can reproduce

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.080
the provider accepting a payment
before returning a timeout.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.440
The test retries with the same key
and checks transfers, journal entries

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.760
and balances. A deliberately
introduced duplicate-debit fault

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.080
should make the test fail.
A green build alone is insufficient.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:26.960
Now look at AI applications
at the top right.

00:02:27.088 --> 00:02:29.440
This is a second entry into assurance.

00:02:29.653 --> 00:02:32.720
If the bank changes
an AI assistant or agent,

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:36.680
its versioned application
configuration enters evaluation.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.680
It is not a required extra step
inside every payment API call.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.800
The evaluation service compares
candidate behavior with independent

00:02:44.871 --> 00:02:47.840
expected results on held-out cases.

00:02:47.936 --> 00:02:51.600
Held-out means those cases
were reserved for assessment,

00:02:51.646 --> 00:02:55.600
rather than used to tune the candidate.
Human reviewers label

00:02:55.648 --> 00:03:00.000
important examples and calibrate
any model-based judges.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.640
For an AI failure-summary assistant, check
whether its explanation matches the raw

00:03:04.704 --> 00:03:08.920
test evidence. It must not turn
a failed assertion into a pass.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.360
Sandbox checks and applicable AI
evaluations send their evidence

00:03:13.387 --> 00:03:17.760
to the release authority. The accountable
reviewer uses existing pipeline

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:21.680
and change gates to approve,
hold or roll back.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:26.040
Missing evidence or a failed critical
payment assertion means hold.

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:29.440
The agent that generated
the change cannot approve itself.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:33.840
The evidence store retains run
identifiers, input versions,

00:03:33.893 --> 00:03:37.760
proposed artifacts, raw results
and the release decision.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:42.880
The dashed arrows represent these
context and evidence relationships,

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.360
not another execution sequence.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.680
For the retry scenario, a reviewer
should be able to trace the one-transfer

00:03:49.752 --> 00:03:53.000
assertion back to its rule
and reproduce the run.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:58.560
Finally, people curate useful
failures into the regression corpus.

00:03:58.656 --> 00:04:02.640
Each accepted case has a reviewed
expectation and a version.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:06.560
The feedback path challenges
later AI application versions.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.560
Keep assessment cases
separate from tuning examples,

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.400
and maintain payment regression
tests in the normal test repository.

00:04:14.516 --> 00:04:19.280
Learning is reviewed curation,
not automatic acceptance of model output.

00:04:19.504 --> 00:04:23.680
This depends on repeatable
environments, controlled test data,

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:28.160
service virtualization,
reliable pipelines and named owners.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.960
Where vendor test slots are scarce,
controlled substitutes expand repeatable

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:37.120
testing; separate checks against
the real provider remain necessary.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:41.120
The outcome to demonstrate
is a repeatable payment test,

00:04:41.173 --> 00:04:44.960
an independently detected
fault and a traceable decision.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.880
AI assists the work. Modernized
testing makes it dependable.
